         "children": [
          {
           "t": "heading",
           "level": "h2",
           "text": "What Makes a Clothing Brand Logo Work?",
           "classes": []
          },
          {
           "t": "text",
           "html": "<p>A <strong>clothing line logo</strong> must look good as a design element on the product itself, not only on a website. It appears on chest prints, neck labels, hat fronts and hang tags, often at very small sizes or stitched in thread, so it must be distinctive and technically simple enough to reproduce.</p><p>Most apparel brands need a primary logo plus a compact mark, such as a monogram or icon, for labels, tags and embroidery.</p>",
           "classes": []
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
